<!--
  model.sdf.xacro

  Xacro source for the Gazebo model. Generated into models/spot/model.sdf at
  build time (see CMakeLists.txt); the world files' existing
  <include><uri>package://spot_description_sim/models/spot</uri></include>
  keeps working unchanged.

  Frame offsets shared with the TF tree (urdf/spot.urdf.xacro) come from
  urdf/spot_frame_properties.xacro, so the numbers exist in exactly one place.
  Physics-only content (inertials, joint dynamics, PID gains, collision
  tuning) is intentionally sim-specific and lives here.

  Intended deviations from the previous hand-written model.sdf (everything
  else is verified equivalent by scripts/verify_model_alignment.py):
    1. front_left leg normalized to match the other three legs:
       - removed the stray inertial <pose> on front_left_hip that placed its
         CoM ~0.30 m outboard of the joint (the other three hips have no
         inertial pose),
       - foot contact sphere radius 0.04 -> 0.036 (value used by the other
         three legs).
    2. <gz_frame_id> added to the five fisheye cameras and the IMU so bridged
       messages carry TF-resolvable frame_ids (the gpu_lidar already did this).
    3. *_ee frames moved from z=-0.3365 to z=-0.37 below the knee, matching
       the URDF value CHAMP has always used (no Gazebo consumer of these
       frames; they are massless welded bodies).
    4. Derived arm frame poses replace hand-rounded constants (differences
       are below 0.1 mm).
-->
